<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1509–<a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada was a Spanish lawyer and conquistador who in 1536 led an expedition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-marta">Santa Marta</a> up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdalena-river">Magdalena River</a> into the highlands of the Muisca. He defeated the zipa of Bacatá and the zaque of Hunza, plundered the Sun Temple at Sogamoso in Iraca, and in 1538 founded Santafé de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> as capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. He later led a fruitless search for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-dorado">El Dorado</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gonzalo-jimenez-de-quesada.jpg" alt="Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ricardo Gómez Campuzano · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Licenciado_Gonzalo_Jim%C3%A9nez_de_Quesada.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1537 fewer than 180 survivors of <b>Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</b>'s expedition, with horses and steel, overcame much larger Muisca forces, seized the zaque at Hunza and drove the zipa Tisquesusa into the hills, where he died of a wound.</blockquote><a href="/empire/muisca-confederation">Muisca Confederation · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Spanish conquistadors led by <b>Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</b> subjected Bacatá, the main settlement of a Muisca confederation and seat of the zipa, ruler of the Bogotá savanna.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-20">20 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Spanish troops under <b>Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</b> reached Sugamuxi in 1537, and the Temple of the Sun burned down while soldiers looted it.</blockquote><a href="/state/iraca">Iraca</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</b> led an expedition up the Magdalena river and conquered the Muisca between 1537 and 1539.</blockquote><a href="/state/new-kingdom-of-granada">New Kingdom of Granada</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1537 <b>Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</b> seized Hunza and captured the aged zaque Quemuenchatocha.</blockquote><a href="/state/zacazgo-of-hunza">Zacazgo of Hunza</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</b> entered the savanna in 1537.</blockquote><a href="/state/zipazgo-of-bacata">Zipazgo of Bacatá</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in Mariquita, in what is now <a href="/countries/colombia">Colombia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=37.18,-3.6&amp;year=1554" aria-label="Granada on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4460 825 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4910 1095h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4910 1095h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=37.18,-3.6&amp;year=1554">What was here in 1554? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
